       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 4250 mg three times daily is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day (some references say 2,000\u20133,000 mg/day). The maximum single dose is about 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** The ordered amount is about 5 times the daily maximum. It could cause severe lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Common intended doses include:\n- 425 mg TID, though this isn't a standard tablet strength.\n- 850 mg TID (2,550 mg/day), which is the max dose.\n- 500 mg TID or 1,000 mg BID.\n\nWhat dose did you intend? I'd also suggest checking it with your resident or attending, and with pharmacy if needed. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order right away. I'll add a note to give it with meals."
