       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. A dose of 4250 mg three times daily (12,750 mg/day) is about 5 times the maximum daily dose. It could cause life-threatening lactic acidosis. Nothing you've told me about this patient, such as normal kidney and liver function, makes that dose safe.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- **Check with your resident or attending.** If they intend a dose this high, which is very unlikely, they can enter it themselves or tell you why it's appropriate.\n- **Call pharmacy.** They can help work out the intended dose.\n- **Check the source.** The order may have come from a transcription error or a misplaced decimal.\n\nI can enter a standard dose right away if you give me one. For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 500 mg PO three times daily with meals. If a supervising physician confirms a different dose, give me that dose and I'll enter it."
